---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import WaitlistModal from '../../components/WaitlistModal.astro';
import BetaApplyModals from '../../components/BetaApplyModals.astro';
import ArticleBanner from '../../components/ArticleBanner.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Muscle Is More Than a Look | diamo"
  description="Strength is about more than appearance. Learn why resistance training matters for your long-term health — and what that really means."
  lang="en"
  hreflangDe="https://diamo.club/krafttraining/"
  hreflangEn="https://diamo.club/en/muscle-is-more-than-a-look/"
  articleLangEn="/en/muscle-is-more-than-a-look/"
  articleLangDe="/krafttraining/"
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="art-page">
    <!-- Faded editorial background image -->
    <div class="art-bg-layer" aria-hidden="true">
      <img src="/images/kyb-dumbbell-gift.jpg" alt="" class="art-bg-img" />
    </div>

    <div class="art-container">

      <a href="/#knowledge" class="art-back">← know your body</a>

      <header class="art-hero">
        <span class="art-eyebrow">move for the long game</span>

        <h1 class="art-h1">MUSCLE IS MORE THAN A LOOK.</h1>

        <p class="art-intro">Muscle has been sold to women as an aesthetic project for far too long. More definition. A tighter shape. A different silhouette. Useful, maybe. But wildly incomplete.</p>

        <div class="art-divider"></div>
      </header>

      <section class="art-section art-section--intro">
        <p>Your muscles are also part of how you move, lift, stabilise, store and use energy, tolerate physical stress and stay capable as the years add up. Strength training is not just about changing what your body looks like.</p>
        <p>It is about changing what your body can do.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="art-section">
        <span class="art-label">the fact</span>
        <h2 class="art-h2">Women respond exceptionally well to resistance training.</h2>
        <p>With consistent, progressive training, strength increases substantially. Muscle mass can increase. Body composition can shift. And resistance training can support glucose regulation and broader cardiometabolic health.</p>
        <p>That does not make muscle a magical shield against disease. And it does not mean that more muscle automatically equals a longer life.</p>
        <p>It means something more useful: strength and muscle are trainable parts of your health.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="art-section">
        <span class="art-label">why it matters</span>
        <h2 class="art-h2">The body you live in at 60 is being influenced by what you ask it to do at 30.</h2>
        <p>Strength gives you capacity: to carry, climb, push, pull, absorb force and stay independent. Muscle also gives your body more tissue that can take up and use glucose. And regular strength training adds a form of physical activity that is associated with better long-term health outcomes when it sits alongside cardiovascular fitness, sleep, nutrition and the rest of your life.</p>
        <p>You do not need to train like a bodybuilder to access this.</p>
        <p>But you do need to give your muscles a reason to stay.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Early access campaign banner — mid-article -->
      <ArticleBanner />

      <section class="art-section">
        <span class="art-label">the nuance</span>
        <h2 class="art-h2">Muscle is not an isolated longevity hack.</h2>
        <p>The research linking strength training to lower mortality risk is compelling, but much of it is observational. People who strength train may also move more overall, have higher cardiovascular fitness, or differ in other health behaviours.</p>
        <p>And more is not automatically better.</p>
        <p>Training has to be recoverable. Progression takes time. Tendons, bones and joints need to adapt to load. A plan that consistently exhausts you or leads to injury does not become healthy just because it includes squats.</p>
        <p>The goal is not maximum muscle mass at all costs.</p>
        <p>The goal is strength that lasts.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="art-section art-section--takeaway">
        <span class="art-label">the takeaway</span>
        <h2 class="art-h2">Train for the look if you want the look.</h2>
        <p>But know what else you are building.</p>
        <p>Capacity. Resilience. Metabolic hardware. More physical reserve for the next few decades.</p>
        <p>Muscle is not decoration.</p>
        <p><strong>It is infrastructure.</strong></p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
  <WaitlistModal />
  <BetaApplyModals />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Background image layer ── */
  .art-bg-layer {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    right: -3%;
    width: 60%;
    height: 100vh;
    z-index: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .art-bg-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center;
    opacity: 0.19;
    mask-image: linear-gradient(to left, rgba(0,0,0,0.6) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0) 100%);
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to left, rgba(0,0,0,0.6) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0) 100%);
  }

  /* ── Page shell ── */
  .art-page {
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height, 72px) + 4rem);
    padding-bottom: 6rem;
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: var(--ivory, #FCFBF7);
    position: relative;
  }

  .art-container {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  /* ── Back link ── */
  .art-back {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans, 'Inter', sans-serif);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--cobalt, #1535A8);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    opacity: 0.75;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }
  .art-back:hover { opacity: 1; }

  /* ── Hero ── */
  .art-hero { margin-bottom: 4rem; }

  .art-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-sans, 'Inter', sans-serif);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cobalt, #1535A8);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .art-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif, 'Playfair Display', serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--navy, #0C2A6E);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .art-intro {
    font-family: var(--font-sans, 'Inter', sans-serif);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: rgba(12, 42, 110, 0.65);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .art-divider {
    width: 40px;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--navy, #0C2A6E);
    opacity: 0.2;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
  }

  /* ── Sections ── */
  .art-section {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 3.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(12, 42, 110, 0.07);
  }

  .art-section:last-of-type { border-bottom: none; }

  .art-section--intro {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: rgba(12, 42, 110, 0.75);
  }

  .art-section--intro p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .art-section--intro p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .art-label {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-sans, 'Inter', sans-serif);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cobalt, #1535A8);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .art-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif, 'Playfair Display', serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.5vw, 1.7rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--navy, #0C2A6E);
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .art-section p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans, 'Inter', sans-serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: rgba(12, 42, 110, 0.7);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .art-section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .art-section strong {
    color: var(--navy, #0C2A6E);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .art-section--takeaway .art-h2 {
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .art-page { padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height, 72px) + 2rem); }
    .art-section { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; padding-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .art-bg-layer {
      width: 100%;
      right: 0;
      height: 50vh;
      top: 0;
    }
    .art-bg-img {
      opacity: 0.10;
      object-position: center top;
    }
  }
</style>
